 "definition": "Net gain share = (taxes the Ukrainian state collects on producing/exporting the good: profit tax, subsoil rent, export duties, land tax/single tax and other non-labour production taxes) + (operating profit above a normal return on capital), divided by the export price (FOB). Counted along the whole Ukrainian value chain (farm + trader for grain; farm + crusher + duty for oilseeds; mill + upstream Ukrainian ore for steel). Not counted: wages and labour taxes (PIT, military levy, social contribution - they are part of the wage), materials, fuel, energy, logistics (rail, trucks, Danube/port charges, war-risk costs), depreciation, land lease payments to landowners, VAT (exports are zero-rated), and a normal return on capital employed (round 14b: 23.0% a year after tax in nominal USD on book capital, low case 24.0%, high case 22.0%: 5% real (4-6%) + Ukraine's country risk premium 15.54% + 2.5% expected USD inflation; the stage formula subtracts r_pre = r / (1 - tau) from the pre-tax margin). Stage formula: s*[t_other + tau*E(max(m,0)) + (1-tau)*E(max(m - r*k, 0))], where s = stage revenue/FOB, m = EBIT/stage revenue (after rent and production taxes), k = capital/stage revenue, r = normal return, tau = profit-tax rate; E(max(.)) taken over a normal spread of firm margins (sd given) so that profitable firms still count when the average firm breaks even. Values are shares of FOB value, 0..1. 2026 = January-August.",
